invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh poly1305-avx2
reason: each round of carries keeps word 0's low 26 bits and drops 5
  times the carry out of word 4, so every group loses the part of its sums
  above 2^130 that is 5 modulo 2^130 - 5. The tag is wrong for every
  update the kernel takes past one group. Only an x86-64 compiler reads
  the line, so the script builds bin/poly1305_equiv_test for x86-64 and
  runs it under qemu-x86_64.

--- old
    out[0] = sums_add_carry_times_5(sums_low_word(in[0]), in[4]);
--- new
    out[0] = sums_low_word(in[0]);
